CORE
array_of_structs_copy1.sv

^\[main\.p1\] .*: PROVED \(transition property\)$
^\[main\.p2\] .*: PROVED \(transition property\)$
^\[main\.p3\] .*: PROVED \(transition property\)$
^\[main\.p4\] .*: PROVED \(transition property\)$
^\[main\.p5\] .*: REFUTED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A copy of an entire packed array of packed structs, after a loop has
written its elements as a whole. The copy used to be wrong. The
elements are compared one by one, as the SMT back-ends refute the
equality of entire packed arrays (see array_of_structs_loop1).
